Description: Offline forensic explorer for container runtimes
 Container Explorer is a standalone utility for exploring and analyzing
 container runtimes (containerd, Docker, and Podman) completely offline
 without running container daemons.
 .
 It parses metadata databases and storage layers directly on disk, supporting
 listing containers/images/tasks, inspecting OCI specs, mounting container
 filesystems, detecting filesystem drift, and exporting container filesystems.
